Independent metric-energy and force audit: 2 x 3 degrees, 2 x 2 knot spans, nonrigid curved surface
StaticStructural nsteps 1 deltat 1.0 rtolv 1.e-11 maxiter 25 manrmsteps 1 nmodules 1
errorcheck
domain 3d
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all element_all
ndofman 20 nelem 1 ncrosssect 1 nmat 1 nbc 21 nic 0 nltf 1 nset 20
# A doubly curved surface in a general global orientation, with degrees (p,q)=(2,3), four nonuniform
# knot spans, and a nonrigid displacement in all three directions. Every displacement is prescribed
# except w of control point 11; its applied force gives the known target w=0.032399981732271294.
# This exercises the assembled nonlinear tangent on a curved surface, rather than only rigid motion.
#
# Independent references: Cox-de Boor basis derivatives, 4 x 4 Gauss quadrature on each span, and
# five-point differences of the total membrane energy with h=1e-4 in each control-point displacement.
# The energy is integrated from the reference/current metrics A_ab and a_ab, independently of BH:
# J=sqrt(det(a)/det(A)), |F|^2=A^ab a_ab, and
# W=.4 J+.2 |F|+.5 (|F|^2/2-1-ln J)+.6 (ln J)^2/2+.3 (J-1)^2/2.
# Reactions and the applied force below are these energy derivatives, not fitted solver outputs;
# the original independent OOFEM comparison differed by at most 6e-12. The check tolerance is absolute.
# checktangent also compares the material tangent to admissible surface finite differences.
